{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-torus-embeddable-complete","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:torus-embeddable-complete","kind":"proposition","title":"Completeness of torus knots embeddable in the Bring's surface","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/thm-embeddability-closure"],"examples":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-archimedean-chirality","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-light-cone-affine","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-chirality-trefoil","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-linking-relations-table","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-chirality-trefoil-electron-positron","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-unmapped-torus-knots","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-force-knot-identification","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-diophantine-valley","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/ex-archimedean-yekutieli"],"tags":["torus-knot","embeddability","genus","completeness","seifert-genus","brings-surface"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Archimedean.torus_embeddable_complete","text":"torus-embeddable-complete.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/torus-embeddable-complete.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:torus-embeddable-complete\"></a><p>The generator set <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{G}</code> is exactly the complete list of torus knots embeddable in the genus-<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">4</code> fiber of Bring's surface. Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T_{m,n}</code> be a torus knot with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\gcd(m,n) = 1</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">1 &#x3C; m &#x3C; n</code>. It embeds in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Sigma_4</code> if and only if <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(m,n)</code> belongs to:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\{(2,3),(2,5),(2,7),(2,9),(3,4),(3,5)\\}.</code></pre>\n<p>Together with the unknot <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T_{1,0}</code>, these are the only localized torus knots in the Descartes universe.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/torus-embeddable-complete.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"7.12.7"}
